It is Saturday morning.
I leave my flat.
Sabine is standing on the stairs.
Bruno is with her.
"Good morning, Maya," Sabine says.
"Good morning, Sabine," I say.
"I have time today."
"I want to see the city."
"Go to Museum Island," she says.
"But do not take the U-Bahn."
"Take the tram."
"From the tram you see a lot of the city."
"It goes almost all the way to the museums."
"Get off at Friedrichstraße," Sabine says.
"From there the way is short."
"Thank you, Sabine," I say.
"That is a great plan."
I go downstairs to the street.
